.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt PATINA-NOTIFY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-notify
.Nd the Patina desktop's notification daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows apps' notifications as cards down the right edge of the screen, one under
another, newest last.
Each card has the app's name, a close button in its top right corner, a summary,
a body and a button for each action the app offered; clicking the card itself
sends the app its default action and brings the app's window forward; the card
closes only if a window came forward.
Cards stay until they are dismissed, unless the app gave the notification a
timeout; critical ones never expire.
.Pp
While any card is showing the column keeps its space, as the bar does, and tiled
and maximised windows make room for it.
While a fullscreen window has the keyboard, a game or a video, they wait and
show again when it is left.
.Pp
It takes the name
.Li org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus, so it stops with an error where another notification daemon
already has it, as GNOME's does.
.Xr patina-compositor 1
keeps it running in the session.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin to wear, as the bar sets it; otherwise the bar's config's.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-notify/config.toml
Looked at once a second; the bell in the tray and Settings' Notifications page write it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li enabled = false
turns notifications off: nothing is shown and no space is kept, though the
calls apps make still succeed.
.It Li hide_in_fullscreen = false
shows notifications while a fullscreen window has the keyboard; by default they
wait until it is left.
.El
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl notify-send -u critical -A open=Open Updates \&"15 updates can be applied\&"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr notify-send 1 ,
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
